const o={toc:[{id:"what-is-body-polishing",text:"What Is Body Polishing?",level:2},{id:"the-key-body-polishing-benefits",text:"The Key Body Polishing Benefits",level:2},{id:"1-removes-dull-dry-surface-skin",text:"1. Removes dull, dry surface skin",level:3},{id:"2-softer-smoother-feeling-skin",text:"2. Softer, smoother-feeling skin",level:3},{id:"3-a-natural-healthy-looking-glow",text:"3. A natural, healthy-looking glow",level:3},{id:"4-a-relaxing-self-care-ritual",text:"4. A relaxing self-care ritual",level:3},{id:"5-skin-thats-ready-for-events-and-outfits",text:"5. Skin that's ready for events and outfits",level:3},{id:"full-body-polish-vs-area-polish",text:"Full Body Polish vs Area Polish",level:2},{id:"areas-you-can-choose",text:"Areas you can choose",level:3},{id:"what-happens-during-a-full-body-polish",text:"What Happens During a Full Body Polish?",level:2},{id:"when-to-book-a-body-polish",text:"When to Book a Body Polish",level:2},{id:"timing-for-events",text:"Timing for events",level:3},{id:"body-polish-and-waxing-get-the-timing-right",text:"Body Polish and Waxing: Get the Timing Right",level:2},{id:"before-your-body-polish",text:"Before Your Body Polish",level:2},{id:"body-polish-aftercare",text:"Body Polish Aftercare",level:2},{id:"body-polishing-vs-other-treatments",text:"Body Polishing vs Other Treatments",level:2},{id:"body-polish-offers",text:"Body Polish Offers",level:2},{id:"how-often-should-you-get-a-body-polish",text:"How Often Should You Get a Body Polish?",level:2},{id:"a-note-on-sensitive-skin",text:"A Note on Sensitive Skin",level:2},{id:"questions-to-ask-when-you-book",text:"Questions to Ask When You Book",level:2},{id:"common-mistakes",text:"Common Mistakes",level:2},{id:"body-polish-for-different-skin-types",text:"Body Polish for Different Skin Types",level:2},{id:"making-your-glow-last",text:"Making Your Glow Last",level:2},{id:"book-your-body-polish-in-bangalore",text:"Book Your Body Polish in Bangalore",level:2}],before:`<p>We put a lot of care into our faces, but the skin on our arms, legs and back often gets forgotten. Sun, pollution and dryness leave it looking dull and feeling rough. A body polish is the body&#39;s equivalent of a good facial, and the <strong>body polishing benefits</strong> are simple: softer, smoother, glowing skin from head to toe.</p>
<p>This guide explains what body polishing is, what happens during a session, the occasions it&#39;s perfect for, and how to look after your skin afterwards.</p>
<h2 id="what-is-body-polishing">What Is Body Polishing?</h2>
<p>Body polishing is a body treatment that gently exfoliates dull, dry skin with a scrub, then polishes and moisturises it. The result is skin that looks and feels smoother, softer and visibly glowing.</p>
<p>At Xing Premium Unisex Salon, our <a href="/services/body-polish">body polish</a> is available for women, at all our salons in Bangalore.</p>
<h2 id="the-key-body-polishing-benefits">The Key Body Polishing Benefits</h2>
<h3 id="1-removes-dull-dry-surface-skin">1. Removes dull, dry surface skin</h3>
<p>The scrub gently lifts away the dull, dry surface skin that builds up on arms, legs and the back, especially after sun exposure.</p>
<h3 id="2-softer-smoother-feeling-skin">2. Softer, smoother-feeling skin</h3>
<p>Once the dull surface layer is gone, skin feels noticeably softer and smoother to touch.</p>
<h3 id="3-a-natural-healthy-looking-glow">3. A natural, healthy-looking glow</h3>
<p>Polished, moisturised skin reflects light better, so it looks fresher and more radiant.</p>
<h3 id="4-a-relaxing-self-care-ritual">4. A relaxing self-care ritual</h3>
<p>A full body polish is genuinely relaxing, especially with the complimentary head massage. Many clients book it simply as time for themselves.</p>
<h3 id="5-skin-thats-ready-for-events-and-outfits">5. Skin that&#39;s ready for events and outfits</h3>
<p>Sleeveless blouses, backless outfits, dresses and holiday wear all show more skin. A body polish leaves that skin looking its best.</p>
<h2 id="full-body-polish-vs-area-polish">Full Body Polish vs Area Polish</h2>
<p>You can choose a full body polish or polish only the areas you want.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th>Full Body Polish</th>
<th>Area Polish</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td><strong>What you get</strong></td>
<td>Complete head-to-toe care</td>
<td>Targeted care for specific areas</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Includes</strong></td>
<td>Shower and a complimentary head massage</td>
<td>Scrub, polish and lotion on the areas you choose</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Best for</strong></td>
<td>Events and complete pampering</td>
<td>A quick refresh of specific areas</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
<h3 id="areas-you-can-choose">Areas you can choose</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Underarms:</strong> gentle exfoliation and polish for smoother-feeling, refreshed underarms</li>
<li><strong>Full arms:</strong> polish from shoulders to fingertips, perfect for sleeveless outfits</li>
<li><strong>Back:</strong> care for the area you can&#39;t reach yourself, ideal before backless outfits</li>
<li><strong>Half legs:</strong> polish for the lower legs</li>
<li><strong>Full legs:</strong> full-length leg polish for dresses and holidays</li>
<li><strong>Full body:</strong> the complete experience</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="what-happens-during-a-full-body-polish">What Happens During a Full Body Polish?</h2>
<p>Here&#39;s what to expect step by step:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Consultation:</strong> choose full body or the areas you want polished.</li>
<li><strong>Gentle scrub:</strong> your full body or chosen areas are exfoliated.</li>
<li><strong>Polish:</strong> the skin is polished for a smooth finish.</li>
<li><strong>Shower and cleanse:</strong> included with the full body polish.</li>
<li><strong>Nourishing body lotion:</strong> to leave skin soft and moisturised. With the full body polish, you also get a complimentary head massage.</li>
</ol>
<p>It&#39;s a relaxing experience from start to finish.</p>
<h2 id="when-to-book-a-body-polish">When to Book a Body Polish</h2>
<p>Body polishing is popular for special occasions, but it works just as well as regular self-care.</p>
<p><strong>Perfect for:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Before your wedding or pre-wedding functions</strong></li>
<li><strong>Before a beach holiday</strong></li>
<li><strong>Before parties and festive occasions</strong></li>
<li><strong>Before a photoshoot</strong></li>
<li><strong>A monthly self-care treat</strong></li>
</ul>
<h3 id="timing-for-events">Timing for events</h3>
<p>For an event, book your body polish <strong>one to three days before</strong> the occasion. That gives your skin time to settle while still looking freshly polished on the day. Pair it with a simple hair, skin and nail plan rather than trying several new services at the last minute.</p>
`,after:`<h2 id="body-polish-and-waxing-get-the-timing-right">Body Polish and Waxing: Get the Timing Right</h2>
<p>Many people book waxing and body polish before the same event. To keep your skin comfortable:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Avoid waxing or shaving right before or right after your polish.</strong></li>
<li>Ask us about the best timing when you book.</li>
</ul>
<p>If you&#39;re planning both, our guide to <a href="/blog/waxing-aftercare-ingrown-hairs">waxing aftercare</a> explains how to look after freshly waxed skin.</p>
<h2 id="before-your-body-polish">Before Your Body Polish</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Avoid waxing or shaving</strong> right before your appointment</li>
<li><strong>Wear loose, comfortable clothes</strong></li>
<li><strong>Tell your therapist</strong> if you have sensitive skin, cuts, sunburn or a skin condition, or if you&#39;re pregnant</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="body-polish-aftercare">Body Polish Aftercare</h2>
<p>To keep your skin soft and glowing:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Moisturise daily</strong> to keep skin soft</li>
<li><strong>Use sunscreen</strong> on exposed areas</li>
<li><strong>Avoid waxing or shaving</strong> right after your polish</li>
<li><strong>Drink water</strong> and keep skin hydrated</li>
<li><strong>Avoid very hot showers</strong> that dry the skin</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="body-polishing-vs-other-treatments">Body Polishing vs Other Treatments</h2>
<p>It helps to know what body polishing is, and what it isn&#39;t.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Body polish vs de-tan:</strong> a de-tan treatment helps reduce the look of tan from sun exposure. A body polish focuses on exfoliating, smoothing and moisturising for softer, glowing skin. They&#39;re separate services. Read what a de-tan treatment is to learn more.</li>
<li><strong>Body polish vs waxing:</strong> waxing removes hair; body polishing smooths and refreshes skin. Many people do both before an event, with the timing advice above.</li>
<li><strong>Body polish vs a facial:</strong> a facial cares for the face. A body polish gives the rest of your skin similar attention.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="body-polish-offers">Body Polish Offers</h2>
<p>Every <strong>Full Body Polish</strong> at Xing includes a <strong>complimentary head massage</strong>. You can also use our salon-wide offers, including Tuesday flat 25% off (minimum billing applies), birthday week offers and memberships.</p>
<h2 id="how-often-should-you-get-a-body-polish">How Often Should You Get a Body Polish?</h2>
<p>There&#39;s no fixed rule. Many clients book:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Before events and holidays</strong>, one to three days before</li>
<li><strong>Monthly</strong>, as a self-care treat and to keep skin soft</li>
<li><strong>Seasonally</strong>, for example after summer, when skin feels dry from sun exposure</li>
</ul>
<p>Your therapist can suggest a routine that suits your skin.</p>
<h2 id="a-note-on-sensitive-skin">A Note on Sensitive Skin</h2>
<p>If you have sensitive skin, cuts, sunburn or a skin condition, or you&#39;re pregnant, let your therapist know before your session. They&#39;ll advise you on whether body polishing is suitable and when to book.</p>
<h2 id="questions-to-ask-when-you-book">Questions to Ask When You Book</h2>
<ul>
<li>Which areas would you recommend for my occasion?</li>
<li>How far ahead of my event should I book?</li>
<li>Should I schedule waxing before or after, and how far apart?</li>
<li>Is body polishing suitable for my skin?</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="common-mistakes">Common Mistakes</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Waxing or shaving right before or after your polish</strong></li>
<li><strong>Booking on the same day as a big event,</strong> rather than one to three days before</li>
<li><strong>Skipping moisturiser afterwards,</strong> which lets skin dry out again</li>
<li><strong>Forgetting sunscreen</strong> on polished, exposed skin</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="body-polish-for-different-skin-types">Body Polish for Different Skin Types</h2>
<p><strong>Dry skin:</strong> you&#39;ll notice the biggest difference, as the polish lifts dry, dull skin and the lotion restores softness. Moisturise daily afterwards.</p>
<p><strong>Oily or combination skin:</strong> a polish helps body skin, especially the back, feel smoother and fresher.</p>
<p><strong>Sensitive skin:</strong> tell your therapist first, so they can advise you and adjust the treatment.</p>
<h2 id="making-your-glow-last">Making Your Glow Last</h2>
<p>Moisturise every day, drink plenty of water and protect polished skin from strong sun. A gentle exfoliation once a week between salon visits also keeps skin smooth.</p>
<h2 id="book-your-body-polish-in-bangalore">Book Your Body Polish in Bangalore</h2>
<p>The body polishing benefits are easy to see and feel: smoother, softer skin with a natural glow, plus a relaxing hour for yourself. Whether it&#39;s for a wedding, a holiday or simply because you deserve it, a body polish leaves you feeling refreshed from head to toe.</p>
<p>Book your body polish at Xing Premium Unisex Salon in Sarjapur Road, HSR Layout or Brookfield. Tell us which areas you&#39;d like on WhatsApp and we&#39;ll help you plan your session.</p>
`,takeaways:["Body polishing exfoliates dull, dry skin, then polishes and moisturises it for soft, smooth, glowing skin.","A full body polish at Xing includes a shower, full-body scrub, polish and nourishing lotion, plus a complimentary head massage.","You can also polish just the areas you want: underarms, full arms, back, half legs or full legs.","For events, book your body polish one to three days before.","Avoid waxing or shaving right before or after, and moisturise daily afterwards."],faqs:[{q:"What is body polishing?",a:"Body polishing is a body treatment that exfoliates dull, dry skin with a scrub, then polishes and moisturises it, leaving skin soft, smooth and glowing."},{q:"What's included in a full body polish at Xing?",a:"A shower, a full-body scrub, polish and a nourishing body lotion, plus a complimentary head massage."},{q:"When should I get a body polish before my wedding?",a:"Book your final session one to three days before the occasion. Many brides also start a few weeks earlier for the best glow."},{q:"Is body polishing available for men?",a:"Our body polish service is currently available for female clients only."},{q:"Can I polish just my arms or legs?",a:"Yes. Choose from underarms, full arms, back, half legs or full legs, or go for the full body."}]};export{o as default};
